## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a multi-protocol API platform that bridges REST, GraphQL, and gRPC while handling multi-tenancy, contract versioning, and consistent data mapping for common resources like invoices.

## Key Concepts

- OpenAPI-driven REST surface generation
- GraphQL schema stitching across microservices
- gRPC bridging/translation layer
- Multi-tenancy: tenant_id, per-tenant authentication
- Contract versioning via headers and OpenAPI tags
- Data mapping for resource boundaries (invoice)

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: REST handler delegates to GraphQL or gRPC
async function handleInvoiceRequest(req, res) {
  const tenantId = extractTenantFromJWT(req.headers.authorization);
  const version = req.headers['api-version'] || 'v1';

  // Route to appropriate backend based on protocol
  if (req.path.startsWith('/graphql')) {
    return await graphqlResolver(tenantId, req.body.query, version);
  } else if (req.path.startsWith('/grpc')) {
    return await grpcBridge(tenantId, req.method, req.body, version);
  } else {
    return await restHandler(tenantId, req.path, req.body, version);
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical Saga orchestration, event-sourcing replay, and idempotent handling in a beginner onboarding scenario across bounded contexts.

## Key Concepts

- Saga orchestration across services
- Event-sourcing replay and replay safety
- Idempotency and deduplication with correlationId
- Outbox pattern for reliable commands

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal mapping and dedupe for a simple onboarding Saga
const processedEventIds = new Set();
function onEvent(evt) {
  if (processedEventIds.has(evt.id)) return;
  processedEventIds.add(evt.id);
  const cmd = mapEventToCommand(evt);
  publishToOutbox(cmd);
}
function mapEventToCommand(evt) {
  switch (evt.type) {
    case 'UserCreated': return { type: 'GrantCredit', payload: { userId: evt.payload.userId }, correlationId: evt.correlationId };
    case 'CreditGranted': return { type: 'MarkOnboardDone', payload: { userId: evt.payload.userId }, correlationId: evt.correlationId };
    case 'CreditFailed': return { type: 'RollbackUser', payload: { userId: evt.payload.userId }, correlationId: evt.correlationId };
    default: return null;
  }
}
```

